{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-015",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 15,
  "title": "Job 15",
  "display_title": "Job 15",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 15,
  "sortOrder": 18015,
  "verseCount": 35,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then answered Eliphaz the Temanite, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Should a wise man utter vain knowledge, and fill his belly with the east wind?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Should he reason with unprofitable talk? or with speeches wherewith he can do no good?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Yea, thou castest off fear, and restrainest prayer before God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For thy mouth uttereth thine iniquity, and thou choosest the tongue of the crafty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Thine own mouth condemneth thee, and not I: yea, thine own lips testify against thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Art thou the first man that was born? or wast thou made before the hills?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Hast thou heard the secret of God? and dost thou restrain wisdom to thyself?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "What knowest thou, that we know not? what understandest thou, which is not in us?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "With us are both the grayheaded and very aged men, much elder than thy father.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Are the consolations of God small with thee? is there any secret thing with thee?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Why doth thine heart carry thee away? and what do thy eyes wink at,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "That thou turnest thy spirit against God, and lettest such words go out of thy mouth?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "What is man, that he should be clean? and he which is born of a woman, that he should be righteous?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Behold, he putteth no trust in his saints; yea, the heavens are not clean in his sight.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "How much more abominable and filthy is man, which drinketh iniquity like water?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "I will shew thee, hear me; and that which I have seen I will declare;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Which wise men have told from their fathers, and have not hid it:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Unto whom alone the earth was given, and no stranger passed among them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "The wicked man travaileth with pain all his days, and the number of years is hidden to the oppressor.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "A dreadful sound is in his ears: in prosperity the destroyer shall come upon him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "He believeth not that he shall return out of darkness, and he is waited for of the sword.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "He wandereth abroad for bread, saying, Where is it? he knoweth that the day of darkness is ready at his hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Trouble and anguish shall make him afraid; they shall prevail against him, as a king ready to the battle.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "For he stretcheth out his hand against God, and strengtheneth himself against the Almighty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "He runneth upon him, even on his neck, upon the thick bosses of his bucklers:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Because he covereth his face with his fatness, and maketh collops of fat on his flanks.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "And he dwelleth in desolate cities, and in houses which no man inhabiteth, which are ready to become heaps.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "He shall not be rich, neither shall his substance continue, neither shall he prolong the perfection thereof upon the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "He shall not depart out of darkness; the flame shall dry up his branches, and by the breath of his mouth shall he go away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "Let not him that is deceived trust in vanity: for vanity shall be his recompence.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "It shall be accomplished before his time, and his branch shall not be green.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "He shall shake off his unripe grape as the vine, and shall cast off his flower as the olive.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "For the congregation of hypocrites shall be desolate, and fire shall consume the tabernacles of bribery.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:15:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "They conceive mischief, and bring forth vanity, and their belly prepareth deceit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 15:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:15:35"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
